target/
apps/desktop/gen/android/build/
apps/desktop/gen/android/app/build/
deploy/
.git/
*.db
*.db-*
.DS_Store

# Everything .gitignore keeps out of the repository for secrecy, kept out of
# the build context for the same reason. The build context is the repo root
# (`context: ..` in deploy/docker-compose.yml) and deploy/Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .`, so anything here that is merely gitignored still reaches the
# builder and is baked into the build stage's layer. The final image copies
# only the binary, but that layer survives in the builder cache on the host
# and in any push or `docker save` of an intermediate.
#
# This list is not judgement, it is a copy: `secrets_kept_out_of_the_repository_
# stay_out_of_the_build_context` in crates/server/src/main.rs fails if
# .gitignore grows a secret this file does not have. The three entries that
# were missing when this was written -- .env.local, .history/ and
# docs/security-audit.md -- were all added to .gitignore after .dockerignore,
# which is the whole failure mode.
# `**/` because Docker's matching is not git's: a bare `*.pem` here matches
# only at the context root, while the same line in .gitignore matches at any
# depth. The test below asserts name presence, so without these it would
# report a nested `certs/*.pem` as covered when it is not.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env*.local
**/.history/
**/.impeccable/
docs/security-audit.md
dist/
**/*.key
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
**/*.p12
**/*.pem

# Not a secret, but gitignored, so the test above requires it here too: the
# .pyc files apps/desktop/scripts leaves behind have been committed by
# accident once already.
**/__pycache__/

# Dev-only, and gitignored, so the test above requires it here too. It is also
# the largest thing in the tree by far: `COPY . .` would copy every file of it
# into the builder layer on every build whose cache missed.
**/node_modules/
